            <ArticleTitle>Computed tomography of the heart using thallium-201 in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>707-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thallium-201 emission computed tomography (ECT) was performed in 3 pediatric patients in whom conventional scintigraphy was normal but there was a strong clinical suspicion of myocardial disease. Abnormalities in the distribution of myocardial perfusion appeared sharply. Single photon ECT provides a three dimensional reconstruction which results in greater enhancement since activity in overlying structures does not interfere. Its widespread use is limited only by the cost of the imaging device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
